# IZI SDK (`common/izi_sdk`)

Stub: `.api/common/izi_sdk.lua`. Companion: `.api/game_object.lua` (IZI patches that class).

## Import

```lua
---@type izi_api
local izi = require("common/izi_sdk")
```

The stub header's own example says `---@type enums`. That is wrong — the module class is `izi_api`. Keep the local name `izi`.

## Colon vs dot

- `izi.*` module surface is **dot**: `izi.spell(...)`, `izi.me()`, `izi.cast_safe(spell, target)`.
- `izi_spell` / `izi_item` / `game_object` methods are **colon**: `spell:cast_safe(target)`, `unit:has_buff(id)`.
- Module mirrors take the spell as first arg; methods take it as `self`. `izi.cast_safe(spell, target)` and `spell:cast_safe(target)` are the same call.

Method names are snake_case only. There are no `CAST` / `IsCastable` / camelCase spell aliases.

## Spells

```lua
local frostbolt = izi.spell(116)          -- also izi.spell(id1, id2, ...) or izi.spell({ ids })
local ok, meta = frostbolt:cast_safe(izi.target(), "frostbolt")
```

- Create spell objects **once** at file scope, not per frame.
- `:cast` / `:cast_safe` / `:cast_position` / `:cast_target_if` / `:cast_target_if_safe` return `(boolean, izi_cast_meta)`. Read `meta.reason` on failure; do not invent your own failure codes.
- `:cast_defensive(target, filters?, message?, opts?)` returns **boolean only**.
- `cast_target_if(units, mode, filter, ...)` — `mode` is `"max"` or `"min"`; `filter` returns `number|nil` (nil rejects the unit).
- Empowered/charge casts go through `cast_charge_spell(spell, stage, ...)` with `stage` in `1|2|3|4`.

## Cast options

Options live in `cast_opts` / `unit_cast_opts` / `pos_cast_opts` in the stub. Only use fields declared there (`skip_gcd`, `skip_facing`, `skip_range`, `skip_moving`, `check_los`, `damage_type`, `min_hits`, `aoe_radius`, ...).

Documented defaults worth respecting:

- `check_los` defaults to on; `check_los = false` only skips the pre-filter — the game can still refuse the cast.
- Position casts default `use_prediction = true`; prediction cache default is 0.15s.
- `prediction_type` is `"AUTO"|"ACCURACY"|"MOST_HITS"|number`; `geometry` is `"CIRCLE"|"LINE"|number`. No other string literals.
- Immunity checks always block full immunity; pass `damage_type` to disambiguate, or `skip_immune_check = true` to bypass.
- `defensive_filters` defaults: `block_time = 1`, raw HP 50, incoming HP 40.

## Units

```lua
local me = izi.me()                       -- may be nil; guard before use
if not me then return end
local enemies = izi.enemies(8)            -- (radius?, players_only?)
local t = izi.ts()                        -- target selector slot 1
```

`izi.me()`, `izi.get_player()`, `izi.target()`, `izi.ts(i?)` all return `game_object|nil`. Guard every one.

Prefer the patched unit helpers over hand-rolled loops when IZI is already in the file: `unit:has_buff(spec)`, `unit:debuff_remains(spec)`, `unit:get_health_percentage()` (1..100), `unit:distance()`, `unit:time_to_die()`. `aura_spec` is `number|number[]`.

`*_if` variants of the range/list helpers can include dead or blacklisted units — filter them yourself.

## Items

`izi.item(id)` returns `izi_item|nil`. Methods are colon: `:use_self`, `:use_on`, `:use_at_position` and the `_safe` variants (which take `item_use_opts`, not cast opts).

## Clocks — do not mix

- `izi.now()` / `izi.now_seconds()` / `izi.now_ms()` are core timer values (same source as `core.now()`). Pair with `izi.time_since(seconds)` / `izi.time_until(seconds)`.
- `izi.now_game_time_ms()` is game time. Pair with `izi.time_since_ms(ms)` / `izi.time_until_ms(ms)` — those two are documented as game time.
- Never feed a core-timer value into a `_ms` game-time helper. Name variables so the source is obvious.
- `izi.after(seconds, fn)` returns a cancel function. Keep and call it on unload.

## Lifecycle

`izi.on_update()` is declared as a per-frame SDK update to call once from your own `on_update`. Check whether the plugin you are editing already calls it; do not add a second call.

Event subscriptions (`izi.on_buff_gain`, `on_spell_success`, `on_combat_start`, `on_key_release`, ...) each return an unsubscribe function. Store it.

## Never invent

- Spell/unit/item methods not in the stub, including "obvious" ones like a focus getter.
- Extra `opts` fields, prediction modes, or geometry names.
- Return arity — `:cast_defensive` is boolean, most casts are `(boolean, meta)`.
- FB_Nexus (`_G.FrostByte_Nexus`) APIs. Not part of this stub set.
